<title>JAPAN: TIFFE euroyen down on NCB restructuring report.</title>
<headline>TIFFE euroyen down on NCB restructuring report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>March 27 settlement  prev settlement</p>
<p> TIFFE Euroyen 3M (Z)     99.01		   99.06</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Key December three-month euroyen deposit rate futures ended Thursday's TIFFE day session down following a media report that the Ministry of Finance (MOF) and the Bank of Japan (BOJ) are considering measures to support Nippon Credit Bank (NCB), traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The reported measures were seen as a breakthrough for the bank. Its restructuring would help ease worries about Japan's financial system,&quot; said a city bank trader.</p>
